# Walkthrough — MOT Documentation Architecture

## What Was Built

Created a complete documentation architecture inside `MOT/Docs/` for learning firmware repositories one by one.

**37 new files** across 6 top-level folders:

```
Docs/
├── README.md                                  ← Learning roadmap with status table
├── Architecture/
│   └── MOT_System_Architecture.md             ← Full system diagram, wiring, converters
├── Firmware/
│   ├── MOT-ELVH-STM8/
│   │   ├── FIRMWARE_GUIDE.md                  ← Placeholder + prerequisites
│   │   └── REAL_TIME_EXAMPLES.md              ← Execution trace template
│   ├── MOT-SHT40-STM8/    (same structure)
│   ├── MOT-CONTROLLER-CARD/ (+ FreeRTOS pipeline template)
│   ├── MOT-STM32-BOOTLOADER/ (marked learning-only)
│   ├── MOT-SURGEON-DISP/
│   ├── MOT-RGB-SLAVE/
│   ├── MOT-RGB-TCP/
│   ├── MOT-RGB-DMX/
│   └── XRAY-VIEWER-STM8/
├── Controllers/
│   ├── STM8.md, STM32.md, ESP32.md
├── Protocols/
│   ├── I2C.md, UART.md, SPI.md, PWM_Signal.md
│   ├── Modbus.md, RS485.md, TCP_WiFi.md
└── Fundamentals/
    ├── Serial_Communication_Basics.md          ← Frame formats (8N1, parity, etc.)
    ├── PWM.md, ADC.md, GPIO.md
    ├── Polling_vs_Interrupt_vs_DMA.md
    ├── Timers_and_Counters.md, Clock_System.md
    └── Memory_and_Registers.md
```

---

## Key Documents

### [README.md](file:///c:/Users/oml/Documents/BitBucket/MOT/Docs/README.md)
Learning roadmap with 9-firmware tracking table, links to all docs, and recommended learning order.

### [MOT_System_Architecture.md](file:///c:/Users/oml/Documents/BitBucket/MOT/Docs/Architecture/MOT_System_Architecture.md)
Full system overview with:
- Mermaid architecture diagram (all components and connections)
- ASCII system diagram
- Wiring & converters table (7 connection types)
- STM8→STM32 signal path detail (PWM → 0-10V → voltage divider → ADC 12-bit)
- Data flow diagrams (sensor reading, light control, RGB Modbus)
- Repository map

### [REAL_TIME_EXAMPLES template](file:///c:/Users/oml/Documents/BitBucket/MOT/Docs/Firmware/MOT-ELVH-STM8/REAL_TIME_EXAMPLES.md)
Well-structured execution trace format with phases, register BEFORE/AFTER diagrams, memory states, and timing summaries.

### [MOT-CONTROLLER-CARD REAL_TIME_EXAMPLES](file:///c:/Users/oml/Documents/BitBucket/MOT/Docs/Firmware/MOT-CONTROLLER-CARD/REAL_TIME_EXAMPLES.md)
Execution pipeline for FreeRTOS firmware: `Packet → ISR → Buffer → Queue → Task → Parse → Execute → Response → TX Register`.

